{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingEnergyBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingEnergyBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eCross_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eCross_bar","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L144-L149","doc":"Consequently the full involution negates the crossing energy itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bar_neg_of_both","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bar_neg_of_both","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L133-L142","doc":"**The full bar involution does not separate the two channels: it negates\nboth.**\n\nHence \"bar-even\" and \"bar-odd\" cannot be read against `def:bar-involution`\nitself — against that involution the two channels have the *same* parity.\nThe words are meaningful only relative to a named half, which is what the\nnotation-register disambiguation records. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym_bar","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L129-L131","doc":"**Full involution, antisymmetric channel: odd.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_bar","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L125-L127","doc":"**Full involution, symmetric channel: odd.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L121-L123","doc":"**Diagram half (mirror), antisymmetric channel: even.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L111-L119","doc":"**Diagram half (mirror), symmetric channel: odd.**  Exchanging positive\nand negative crossings negates `E_sym`.\n\nTogether with `eSym_coef` this is the apparent double inversion: the same\nsummand is coefficient-*even* and mirror-*odd*, because the mirror flips the\nmultiplicity `p - m` as well as the weight.  Neither block is wrong; they\nreport parity under different halves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym_coef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym_coef","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L107-L109","doc":"**Coefficient half, antisymmetric channel: odd.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_coef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_coef","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L102-L105","doc":"**Coefficient half, symmetric channel: even.**  Holding the diagram\nfixed, `q ↦ q⁻¹` fixes `E_sym`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sinhW_coef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sinhW_coef","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L95-L100","doc":"The bar-odd weight is negated by the coefficient half `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.coshW_coef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.coshW_coef","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L88-L93","doc":"The bar-even weight is fixed by the coefficient half `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_add_eAsym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eSym_add_eAsym","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L81-L86","doc":"The two channels reconstruct the crossing energy exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eCross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eCross","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L78-L79","doc":"The crossing energy `E_cross = p·q - m·q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eAsym","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L75-L76","doc":"The antisymmetric channel total `E_asym = (p + m)·sinh λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eSym","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L72-L73","doc":"The symmetric channel total `E_sym = (p - m)·cosh λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sinhW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sinhW","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L69-L70","doc":"The bar-odd crossing weight `sinh λ = (q - q⁻¹)/2 = h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.coshW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.coshW","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CrossingEnergyBarParity.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The bar-even crossing weight `cosh λ = (q + q⁻¹)/2 = [2]_q/2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}